From: Magnesium maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: use the numeric SATP CSR with modern assemblers

The vendor context switch code uses the obsolete sptbr assembler alias.
Use CSR_SATP as the rest of the kernel does, allowing current OE binutils.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor BSP code]

--- a/arch/riscv/mm/context.c
+++ b/arch/riscv/mm/context.c
@@ -64,7 +64,7 @@
 	asid = (next->context.asid.counter & SATP_ASID_MASK)
 		<< SATP_ASID_SHIFT;
 
-	csr_write(sptbr, virt_to_pfn(next->pgd) | SATP_MODE | asid);
+	csr_write(CSR_SATP, virt_to_pfn(next->pgd) | SATP_MODE | asid);
 #endif
 
 	flush_icache_deferred(next);
